// @tao-next is the self-hosted form of the navigation stdlib: every nav ships as an ordinary Tao
// declaration bound to a runtime implementation through the same public mechanism a third-party
// package uses. Copy this file, rename the declaration, swap the implementation — no compiler or
// language changes involved. At absorption this becomes the real source of @tao/nav.

// Anything an app can present. `ui` and `nav` are closed roles; the union is the capability.
public type Presentable is ui | nav

// A nav declares its configuration contract in Tao. Property names are ordinary capitalized
// identifiers — a copied nav declares its own — and lowercase words stay language structure.
public nav StackNav {
   Initial ui // the argument-free entry seeded at mount; nav-in-stack entries stay deferred

   // `implement inject <protocol>` binds the declaration to a TS value satisfying the published,
   // versioned TR.NavKind protocol. Package-scope only; apps never implement semantics inline.
   //
   // TR.NavKind contract (conformance suite: TR.testNavKind — a package runs it in its own tests):
   // - mount(config) creates mount state: an ordered occurrence list seeded with Initial
   // - render(mount, taoProps) renders the top occurrence; covered occurrences stay mounted,
   //   hidden, and out of accessibility, preserving their local state
   // - present(mount, presentable, arguments) pushes a fresh occurrence — same value, new entry
   // - dismiss(mount, origin) pops when the origin is the top entry; delegates outward at root
   // - back(mount) pops one entry and reports whether the event was consumed; root-safe no-op
   // - reset(mount) returns to the seeded Initial occurrence
   // - descriptors are immutable; equality is the declaration token plus normalized configuration,
   //   never serialized; occurrence identity is monotonic within one app mount
   // - navigation happens only through these verbs — a kind never drives native navigation itself
   implement inject nav ```ts
      // TODO(implementer): port RuntimeStackNav onto the TR.NavKind protocol and return it.
      return TR.NavKind.todo('StackNav')
   ```
}
